\p \w [So they shot Ahaziah] in|strong="H00413"\w* \w his chariot|strong="H04818"\w* \w on the Ascent|strong="H04608"\w* \w of Gur|strong="H01483"\w*,\f + \fr 9:27 \ft See Syriac, Vulgate, and LXX; Hebrew \fqa “Shoot him, too, in his chariot!” (They did this) on the Ascent of Gur,\f* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w -|strong="H00854"\w* \w near Ibleam|strong="H02991"\w*, \w and he fled|strong="H05127"\w* \w to Megiddo|strong="H04023"\w* \w and died|strong="H04191"\w* \w there|strong="H08033"\w*. \v 28 \w Then his servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w carried him by chariot|strong="H07392"\w* \w to Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and buried|strong="H06912"\w* \w him|strong="H00853"\w* \w with his fathers|strong="H00001"\w* \w in his tomb|strong="H06900"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05973"\w* \w in the City|strong="H05892"\w* \w of David|strong="H01732"\w*.
