\c 18
\s1 Hezekiah Destroys Idolatry in Judah
\p \v 1 \w -|strong="H01961"\w* \w In the third|strong="H07969"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w* \w of the reign|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Hoshea|strong="H01954"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Elah|strong="H00425"\w* \w over Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w Hezekiah|strong="H02396"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Ahaz|strong="H00271"\w* \w became king|strong="H04427"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H03063"\w*. \v 2 \w He was|strong="H01961"\w* \w twenty-five|strong="H06242"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02568"\w* \w years old|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08141"\w* \w when he became king|strong="H04427"\w*, \w and he reigned|strong="H04427"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w twenty-nine|strong="H06242"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08672"\w* \w years|strong="H08141"\w*. \w His mother’s|strong="H00517"\w* \w name|strong="H08034"\w* \w was Abi|strong="H00021"\w*,\f + \fr 18:2 \fqa Abi \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijah\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 29:1.\f* \w the daughter|strong="H01323"\w* \w of Zechariah|strong="H02148"\w*. \v 3 \w And he did|strong="H06213"\w* \w [what was] right|strong="H03477"\w* \w in the eyes|strong="H05869"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w just as|strong="H03605"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w his father|strong="H00001"\w* \w David|strong="H01732"\w* \w had done|strong="H06213"\w*. \v 4 \w -|strong="H01931"\w* \w He removed|strong="H05493"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the high places|strong="H01116"\w*, \w shattered|strong="H07665"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the sacred pillars|strong="H04676"\w*, \w and cut down|strong="H03772"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the Asherah poles|strong="H00842"\w*. \w He also demolished|strong="H03807"\w* \w the bronze|strong="H05178"\w* \w snake|strong="H05175"\w* \w called|strong="H07121"\w* \w Nehushtan|strong="H05180"\w*\f + \fr 18:4 \fqa Nehushtan \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa bronze \ft and also for \fqa snake\ft .\f* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w had made|str