\s1 Isaiah’s Message of Deliverance
\p \v 1 \w On|strong="H01961"\w* \w hearing [this report]|strong="H08085"\w*, \w King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Hezekiah|strong="H02396"\w* \w tore|strong="H07167"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w his clothes|strong="H00899"\w*, \w put on|strong="H03680"\w* \w sackcloth|strong="H08242"\w*, \w and entered|strong="H00935"\w* \w the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*. \v 2 \w And he sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Eliakim|strong="H00471"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w the palace|strong="H01004"\w* \w administrator|strong="H05921"\w*, \w Shebna|strong="H07644"\w* \w the scribe|strong="H05608"\w*, \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and the leading|strong="H02205"\w* \w priests|strong="H03548"\w*, \w all wearing|strong="H03680"\w* \w sackcloth|strong="H08242"\w*, \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H05030"\w* \w Isaiah|strong="H03470"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Amoz|strong="H00531"\w* \v 3 \w to tell|strong="H00559"\w* \w him|strong="H00413"\w*, “\w This is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w Hezekiah|strong="H02396"\w* \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: \w Today|strong="H03117"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02088"\w* \w is a day|strong="H03117"\w* \w of distress|strong="H06869"\w*, \w rebuke|strong="H08433"\w*, \w and disgrace|strong="H05007"\w*; \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w children|strong="H01121"\w* \w have come|strong="H00935"\w* \w to the point of|strong="H05704"\w* \w birth|strong="H04866"\w*, \w but there is no|strong="H00369"\w* \w strength|strong="H03581"\w* \w to deliver them|strong="H03205"\w*. \v 4 \w Perhaps|strong="H00194"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w your God|strong="H00430"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w will hear|strong="H08085"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the words|strong="H01697"\w* \w vvv|strong="H07262"\w* \w of the Rabshakeh|strong="H07262"\w*, \w whom|strong="H00834"\w* \w his master|strong="H00113"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H00804"\w* \w has sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w to defy|strong="H02778"\w* \w the living|strong="H02416"\w* \w God|strong="H00430"\w*, \w and He will rebuke him|strong="H03198"\w* \w for the words|strong="H01697"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w your God|strong="H00430"\w* \w has heard|strong="H08085"\w*. \w Therefore lift up|strong="H05375"\w* \w a prayer|strong="H08605"\w* \w for|strong="H01157"\w* \w the remnant|strong="H07611"\w* \w that still survives|strong="H04672"\w*.”
\p \v 5 \w So the servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w of King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Hezekiah|strong="H02396"\w* \w went|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Isaiah|strong="H03470"\w*, \v 6 \w who|strong="H03470"\w* \w replied|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Tell|strong="H00559"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w your master|strong="H00113"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03541"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: ‘\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w be afraid|strong="H03372"\w* \w of|strong="H06440"\w* \w the words|strong="H01697"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w you have heard|strong="H08085"\w*, \w with which|strong="H00834"\w* \w the servants|strong="H05288"\w* \w of the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H00804"\w* \w have blasphemed|strong="H01442"\w* \w Me|strong="H00853"\w*. \v 7 \w Behold|strong="H02005"\w*, \w I will put|strong="H05414"\w* \w a spirit|strong="H07307"\w* in him \w so that he will hear|strong="H08085"\w* \w a rumor|strong="H08052"\w* \w and return|strong="H07725"\w* \w to his own land|strong="H00776"\w*, \w where|strong="H00776"\w* \w I will cause him to fall|strong="H05307"\w* \w by the sword|strong="H02719"\w*.’”
\s1 Sennacherib’s Blasphemous Letter
\p \v 8 \w When|strong="H03588"\w* \w vvv|strong="H07262"\w* \w the Rabshakeh|strong="H07262"\w* \w heard|strong="H08085"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H00804"\w* \w had left|strong="H05265"\w* \w Lachish|strong="H03923"\w*, \w he withdrew|strong="H07725"\w* \w and found|strong="H04672"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w [the king] fighting|strong="H03898"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w* \w Libnah|strong="H03841"\w*.
\p \v 9 \w Now Sennacherib had been warned|strong="H08085"\w* \w about|strong="H00413"\w* \w Tirhakah|strong="H08640"\w* \w king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Cush|strong="H03568"\w*\w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*:\f + \fr 19:9 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* “\w Look|strong="H02009"\w*, \w he has set out|strong="H03318"\w* \w to fight|strong="H03898"\w* \w against you|strong="H00854"\w*.”
